<title>USA: Conceptronic Inc Q1 shr increases.</title>
<headline>Conceptronic Inc Q1 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the Three Months Ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			  Conceptronic Inc.	WMC    Consolidated(A)</p>
<p> Net Sales		   $3,582,000    $5,394,000  $8,976,000</p>
<p> Cost of Sales		2,662,000     3,998,000   6,660,000</p>
<p> Gross Profit		   920,000     1,396,000   2,316,000</p>
<p> Operating expenses	 1,214,000	 283,000   1,497,000</p>
<p> Depreciation		    62,000	 146,000     208,000</p>
<p> Goodwill Amortization	     --	 196,000     196,000</p>
<p>Net Interest and Other</p>
<p>   Expense			 34,000	  46,000	80,000</p>
<p> Corporate Expenses	    49,000	  49,000	98,000</p>
<p>   Total Expenses	   1,359,000	 720,000   2,079,000</p>
<p> Pre-Tax Income (Loss)    (439,000)	 676,000     237,000</p>
<p> Tax Benefit							381,000</p>
<p> Net Income							 618,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share						   .08</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding						   7,517,000</p>
<p>NOTE - (A) Includes the results of White Cable Construction Corp for the three months ended March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>			    Proforma Income Statements</p>
<p>	     For the Three Months Ended March 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   Conceptronic Inc    WMC     Consolidated</p>
<p> Net Sales		    $3,931,000 $2,424,000    $6,355,000</p>
<p> Cost of Sales		 2,742,000  1,791,000     4,533,000</p>
<p> Gross Profit		  1,189,000    633,000     1,822,000</p>
<p> Operating Expenses	    952,000  201,000(A)    1,153,000</p>
<p> Depreciation		     83,000    120,000	 203,000</p>
<p> Goodwill Amortization	     ---  196,000(B)	196,000</p>
<p>Net Interest and Other</p>
<p>  Expense			   95,000  46,000(C)	 141,000</p>
<p>    Total Expenses	   1,130,000    563,000     1,693,000</p>
<p> Pre-Tax Income		   59,000     70,000	 129,000</p>
<p> Income Tax			    ---     28,000	  28,000</p>
<p> Net Income			 59,000     42,000	 101,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share						   .01</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding						   7,301,000</p>
<p>NOTE - (A) Compensation expense adjusted to reflect current salary arrangements.</p>
<p>(B) Amortization of $15,700,000 of goodwill over 20 years.</p>
<p>(C) No adjustment is made for imputed interest expense on acquisition financing. Debt financing was not utilized for the acquisition.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
